{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"amqpsEndpoint","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"url","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"caPEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clientCertificatePEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clientKeyPEM","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmqpsEndpoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13AmqpsEndpointV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AmqpsEndpoint"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"§22.11 rule 3 is why this is a public, tested function rather than a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paragraph.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" §8b rule 7 cannot be satisfied by a runtime that never sees a URL","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— this SDK bundles no AMQP client — so the SDK hands the integrator the check","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead. Documenting the requirement is precisely the failure contract 1.23","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was written to stop: three SDKs asserting ","type":"text"},{"code":"amqps:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a doc comment above a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call that accepted anything.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it enforces:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The scheme MUST be "},{"code":"amqps:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every other scheme is refused, "},{"code":"amqp:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, and there is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no loopback exception"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (§8b rule 8): this applies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"code":"localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"::1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly as to any other host. §6’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"http:\/\/localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dev carve-out does not extend here, and the server has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no plaintext listener for such an exception to reach."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom CA bundle is supported, because an in-cluster broker’s certificate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is not issued by a public CA — the common case, and it exists so nobody has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a legitimate reason to want rule 4 relaxed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A client certificate and its key are required TOGETHER. Half a client","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity fails closed rather than connecting without the mutual half.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no verification-skip option, under any name. It is the most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reliably misused option in TLS: it appears in a dev compose file, it works,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and it travels unchanged into production, where it turns TLS into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expensive no-op against precisely the attacker TLS exists to stop."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no plaintext fallback. A failed "},{"code":"amqps:\/\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" connection is an error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to surface, not a condition to work around — and this call offers no way to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"express one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"amqpsEndpoint"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"caPEM"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clientCertificatePEM"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clientKeyPEM"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK13AmqpsEndpointV","text":"AmqpsEndpoint"}],"symbolKind":"func","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13amqpsEndpoint_5caPEM017clientCertificateF00g3KeyF0AA05AmqpsD0VSS_SSSgA2HtKF","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"am